This problem can be done in
BRUTE FORCE APPROACH:Selection Sort
BETTER APPPROACH:Counting Sort
OPTIMAL APPROACH:Dutch National Flag Algorithm

Core idea:
---------------
Core Idea:
Find the minimum element in the unsorted portion of the array and swap it with the first element of that portion. Repeat until the array is sorted.


BRUTE FORCE APPROACH:
---------------------

n = list(map(int, input().split()))
size = len(n)
for i in range(size):
    min_index = i
    for j in range(i + 1, size):
        if n[j] < n[min_index]:
            min_index = j
    n[i], n[min_index] = n[min_index], n[i]
print(*n)

TC:O(n²)
SC:O(1)

BETTER APPROACH:
------------------------

n = list(map(int, input().split()))
zeros = n.count(0)
ones = n.count(1)
twos = n.count(2)
index = 0
for i in range(zeros):
    n[index] = 0
    index += 1
for i in range(ones):
    n[index] = 1
    index += 1
for i in range(twos):
    n[index] = 2
    index += 1
print(*n)

TC:O(n)
SC:O(1)

OPTIMAL APPROACH
---------------------

n = list(map(int, input().split()))
low = 0
mid = 0
high = len(n) - 1
while mid <= high:
    if n[mid] == 0:
        n[low], n[mid] = n[mid], n[low]
        low += 1
        mid += 1
    elif n[mid] == 1:
        mid += 1
    else:
        n[mid], n[high] = n[high], n[mid]
        high -= 1
print(*n)

TC:O(n)
SC:O(1)
